{"title":"Westmoor Clinic","sub":"Patients wait three weeks. Build more rooms?","type":"Cost & operations","industry":"Healthcare services","geo":"United Kingdom","diff":1,"fmt":"Interviewer-led","time":"25-30 min","skills":"Capacity · bottleneck · task shifting","prompt":"Westmoor is a private outpatient clinic. Patients wait about three weeks for an appointment, and some go elsewhere. The practice manager wants to convert storage space into four more consultation rooms for $600k. The owners ask whether that will cut waiting times.","clarify":[{"q":"Rooms and hours?","a":"10 consultation rooms, open 9 hours a day. Each appointment holds a room for about 30 minutes, including cleaning and set-up."},{"q":"Doctors?","a":"6 doctors, each seeing patients for about 7 hours a day. Each appointment takes about 20 minutes of doctor time, much of it taking history and measurements."},{"q":"Demand?","a":"About 160 appointment requests a working day."}],"structure":{"root":"How can Westmoor see more patients?","branches":[{"head":"Room capacity","items":["Rooms × hours ÷ time per appointment"]},{"head":"Doctor capacity","items":["Doctors × hours ÷ doctor time per appointment"]},{"head":"Which one limits us?","items":["Compare with demand"]}]},"hypothesis":"More rooms only help if rooms are the constraint. I'd compare room capacity with doctor capacity first.","questions":[{"q":"How many patients a day can the rooms handle, and how many can the doctors see?","exhibit":{"kind":"chart","svg":"<svg xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\" width=\"399.26pt\" height=\"164.94pt\" viewBox=\"0 0 399.26 164.94\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" version=\"1.1\"><defs><style type=\"text/css\">*{stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: butt}</style></defs><g id=\"figure_1\"><g id=\"patch_1\"><path d=\"M 0 164.94 L 399.26 164.94 L 399.26 0 L 0 0 L 0 164.94 z\n\" style=\"fill: none\"/></g><g id=\"axes_1\"><g id=\"patch_2\"><path d=\"M 46.1 139.04 L 392.06 139.04 L 392.06 11.528 L 46.1